 "capability": "doublets",
 "title": "Expression doublets",
 "conclusion": "Leave-one-study-out on 17 real-label datasets, Singlet's expression doublet score has mean AUPRC 0.559, against 0.501 for its previous scorer (better on 15/17) and 0.559 for scDblFinder, a statistical tie without R. On the Kang lanes it reaches 0.585 against 0.544; on lane 2.1 as Singlet counts it, 0.701 against 0.642. Genotype doublets remain the call for pools with two or more donors.",
 "methods": "Data: 17 datasets with experimental doublet labels: Kang 2018 demuxlet genotype calls (lane 2.1 as Singlet counts it from the Singlet pipeline, and the five lanes of Xi & Li 2021 as Cell Ranger counts), cell hashing, MULTI-seq and human-mouse species mixing (Xi & Li 2021, Zenodo 4062232, public count matrices). Only doublets visible to the experiment are labelled. Singlet: singlet.doublets, a gradient-boosted ensemble (300 trees, 15 leaves) over the within-sample ranks of log UMI, log detected genes, the engine's doublet score (doublet_detect.h v7) and four features of the atlas cell-type network (k-NN fraction of simulated doublets in the network's embedding, cross-fitted real-versus-simulated classifier, cell-type entropy, two-centroid fit). The ensemble scoring a dataset was trained on the labels of every dataset of the other studies (leave-one-study-out; the six Kang lanes are one study, the five MULTI-seq sets another, the two 10x hgmm sets a third), each dataset weighing the same, so no number here is on cells the model saw. Competitors: the previous Singlet scorer alone, scDblFinder 1.23 and Scrublet 0.2.3 with defaults, on the same counts; no simulated doublet is part of the evaluation. Metrics: AUPRC and AUROC of each tool's score against the labels, per dataset; pooled values are means over datasets (or over studies) with a bootstrap over datasets. Pooled metrics gate against the best competitor with a tolerance equal to the paired bootstrap half-width; per-dataset AUPRC gates against the previous Singlet scorer. Cost: seconds per 10,000 cells from the study's timings, and for Singlet from the batch job on Kang 2.1 (one V100S GPU, 8 CPU threads, including the engine score). Genotype doublets (prob_doublet) are not compared here; they stay the call for pools with two or more donors.",
 "status": "draft",
 "generated_at": "2026-10-29T18:31:24+00:00",
 "owner": "pipeline-benchmark",
 "singlet": {
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "commit": "cfe5cfa2960bf79caa09f9136c1a92aeaa3865fa",
  "branch": "claude/doublet-score",
